>
<p>A WordPress website audit reviews the public site and the WordPress components included in an authorised scope. Plugin, theme, database and account checks require suitable read-only or supervised access.</p>
<p>AuditWeb quotes WordPress work after reviewing site size, plugin count, custom code, commerce features, hosting access and deliverables. The audit does not authorise updates or active security tests.</p>

<h2 id="why-wordpress-needs-specialist-audits">What makes a WordPress audit different?</h2>
<p>A WordPress audit connects public symptoms to the core, theme, plugin and hosting layers that may produce them. The report should state which layers were accessible and avoid guessing about inaccessible configuration.</p>
<p>Use the broader <a href="/website-audit-services/comprehensive/">comprehensive website audit</a> when the main question spans content, journeys and non-WordPress systems.</p>

<h2 id="plugin-audit">What should the plugin review cover?</h2>
<p>The plugin review should inventory active and inactive plugins, versions, update status, ownership and functional overlap. Changes need a backup, staging plan and separate implementation approval.</p>
<p>WordPress advises keeping core, themes and plugins updated in its official <a href="https://developer.wordpress.org/advanced-administration/security/">security handbook</a>. An update flag identifies work to assess. It does not prove that a plugin caused a current defect.</p>

<h2 id="theme-review">What should the theme and template review cover?</h2>
<p>The review should sample real templates and compare source, rendered output and WordPress configuration where access permits. Relevant evidence can include headings, internal links, canonicals, structured data, assets and child-theme customisations.</p>
<p>Custom code should be reviewed in context. A large DOM or multiple assets can guide investigation but does not establish a universal failure threshold.</p>

<h2 id="security-check">What can the WordPress security review establish?</h2>
<p>The audit can record versions, public configuration, HTTPS, headers, exposed files and agreed account or file-permission evidence. It is not a penetration test or certification.</p>
<p>The official <a href="https://developer.wordpress.org/advanced-administration/security/hardening/">WordPress hardening guide</a> covers updates, passwords, file permissions, database security, backups and monitoring. Apply changes in staging where possible and preserve a recovery path.</p>
<p>Scanning, exploitation, login testing and configuration changes require explicit authorisation and a separate plan.</p>

<h2 id="speed-optimisation">How should WordPress performance be assessed?</h2>
<p>Test representative templates and record both field and lab evidence where available. Investigate hosting response, caching, images, themes, plugins and third-party scripts as possible contributors.</p>
<p>Google defines Core Web Vitals as LCP, INP and CLS in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/core-web-vitals">official guidance</a>. A lab run can reproduce a test condition. It cannot replace real-user field data.</p>

<h2 id="whats-included">What should the WordPress audit deliver?</h2>
<p>The report should contain the agreed inventory, template sample, evidence, findings, recommended fixes and verification steps. It should identify any checks blocked by missing hosting, database or administrator access.</p>
<p>Agree whether the quote includes a walkthrough, developer briefing or staging re-test. Implementation remains separate unless included in writing.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">How much does a WordPress audit cost?</h2>
<p>AuditWeb's basic website audit starts at $297 USD and its comprehensive audit starts at $997 USD. A WordPress review that needs administrator, hosting, database, custom-code, WooCommerce or multisite analysis may require a custom quote.</p>
<p>Provide the public URL, rough page and plugin counts, hosting constraints, custom features and main question. AuditWeb will confirm scope, access, price and delivery date before work starts.</p>
